description:
In repos/goal-host-vessel/src/index.ts, add one deterministic oracle and wire it into the verifier chain.

EDIT 1. The file contains this exact line:

async function verifyGapAggregateReach(goal: string, dig: string): Promise<GoalReachVerdict | null> {

Immediately BEFORE that line, insert exactly:

function parseGapTotalCount(goal: string): { status: "open" | "closed" } | null {
  if (!/\b(?:gaps?|substrate\s?gaps?)\b/i.test(goal)) return null;
  if (!/\b(?:how many|count|number of|total)\b/i.test(goal)) return null;
  if (parseGapCategoryAggregate(goal)) return null;
  if (parseGapRatio(goal)) return null;
  return { status: /\bclosed\b/i.test(goal) ? "closed" : "open" };
}

async function verifyGapTotalCountReach(goal: string, dig: string): Promise<GoalReachVerdict | null> {
  const p = parseGapTotalCount(goal);
  if (!p) return null;
  const counts = await fetchGapCategoryCounts(p.status);
  if (!counts) return null;
  let total = 0;
  for (const n of counts.values()) total += n;
  const nums = [...dig.matchAll(/\b(\d{1,6})\b/g)].map((m) => Number(m[1]));
  if (nums.some((n) => Math.abs(n - total) <= 2)) {
    return { reached: true, reason: `deterministic:verified-gap-total - independently recounted the live gap store: ${p.status} gaps = ${total}; the produced output states this value (+/-2 live-drift tolerance)`, deterministic: true, completion_shapes: [] };
  }
  return null;
}

EDIT 2. The file contains this exact block:

  {
    const gapV = await verifyGapAggregateReach(goal, dig);
    if (gapV) return gapV;
  }

Immediately after that block, insert exactly:

  {
    const gapTotalV = await verifyGapTotalCountReach(goal, dig);
    if (gapTotalV) return gapTotalV;
  }

Change nothing else in the file.

Facts, each stated positively:
1. A plain total-gap-count question has a verifier only after this change. verifyGapAggregateReach owns the category extremum and verifyGapRatioReach owns percentages.
2. fetchGapCategoryCounts and parseGapCategoryAggregate and parseGapRatio already exist in this file.
3. This oracle returns null whenever the output states no matching number, so it adds reaches and never adds refusals.
4. I applied both edits locally and verified: tsc --noEmit exits 0, and bun test reports 847 pass and 0 fail.
5. I probed the result against the live gap store: a digest reading "Open Gaps: 621" returned reached true with reason "independently recounted the live gap store: open gaps = 622", accepted by the drift tolerance.
6. A digest naming gaps without a count returned null, and a digest stating 999 returned null.

